'' A WIDE CHAIN INITIALISING A 'zstring * N' OR 'string * N' TRANSCODES. The declaration,
'' the array initialiser and the field initialiser each asked TermIsWide_ whether the
'' value was wide, and TermIsWide_ answers for no chain -- Check types '&' STRING -- so
'' 'dim z as zstring * 20 = w & "d"' went to the narrow path, declined, and z held
'' whatever the frame held. Assigning the same chain afterwards was right. An array
'' initialiser had no wide arm at all, and '( w & "d" )' in parentheses reached the
'' wide path as an N_PAREN it did not look inside. Measured, fbc:
''
''     dim z1 as zstring * 20 = w & "d"   fb_WstrAssignToA_Init( Z1, 20ll, TMP, 0ll )
''     dim f1 as string * 8 = w & "d"     fb_WstrAssignToA_Init( F1, <tagged 8>, TMP, -1ll )
''     { w & "d", "e" & w }               one fb_WstrAssignToA_Init per element
''
'' This file had four statements not lowered.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/wide-chain-to-fixed-init.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrAssignToA_Init(@z1, 20,
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrAssignToA_Init(@f1,
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrAssignToA_Init(@zp, 20,
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrAssignToA_Init(%
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrAssign(@z
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_StrInit(@z
